course: dictionary
lesson: 13836
title: Words from history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: History books use words you may never have met before. Context clues help: the words and sentences around the word show you what it means. «The janissaries guarded the sultan's palace.» Guards protect a place, so a janissary must be a soldier.
explain: «Boys from Christian families in the Balkans were taken and trained to become janissaries.» This tells you the janissaries were trained soldiers in an army. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «The janissary band played loud drums as the army marched.» A band here is a group of musicians, not a group of people tied together. The clue is the drums, and the marching army.
fact: A janissary was a soldier in the elite foot army of the Ottoman (Turkish) sultans.
fact: The janissaries served the sultans from about the 1300s to 1826.
fact: «Janissary» can also mean a loyal follower or guard who does whatever a powerful leader wants, but this meaning is rare.
fact: A janissary band was a group of musicians who played for the army.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The janissaries guarded the sultan's palace.» What is a janissary? | A tall tower built of stone | *A soldier in the Ottoman sultan's army | A queen who ruled a castle | A farmer who grew wheat in the Balkans
exercise: «The janissary band played loud drums as the army marched.» What was the janissary band? | A river crossing | *A group of musicians | A team of cooks | A stone wall
exercise: «The boys were taken and trained for the army.» Which word means taught the skills for a job? | boys | army | taken | *trained
test: In a history lesson, what is the janissary corps? | A ship of the Ottoman navy | *The elite foot army of the Ottoman sultans | A school for cooks | A band that played in the streets of London
test: In the lesson, what does foot army mean? | Soldiers who ride horses | *Soldiers who fight on foot | Soldiers who sail ships | Soldiers who fly planes
exam: Pupil says a janissary is a type of bird. What is the right answer? | A horse ridden by sultans | *A soldier in the Ottoman sultan's army | A type of bird that lives in the Balkans | A stone used to build palaces
